          "confidence": "EXACT",
          "pageNumber": 3,
          "text": "the build list · @1nska\n3"
        },
        {
          "bbox": [
            71.2,
            67.39,
            409.3,
            93.26
          ],
          "blockIndex": 1,
          "blockType": "project_boundary_heading",
          "confidence": "EXACT",
          "pageNumber": 3,
          "text": "STEP 04\nLearn to solder early. It's easier than it looks."
        },
        {
          "bbox": [
            71.2,
            96.9,
            512.8,
            119.83
          ],
          "blockIndex": 2,
          "blockType": "paragraph",
          "confidence": "EXACT",
          "pageNumber": 3,
          "text": "DO THIS\nA $20 temperature-controlled iron, 0.8 mm leaded or lead-free solder, flux and a"
        },
        {
          "bbox": [
            71.2,
            121.67,
            540.4,
            147.43
          ],
          "blockIndex": 3,
          "blockType": "paragraph",
          "confidence": "EXACT",
          "pageNumber": 3,
          "text": "practice kit (a $5 through-hole 'skill kit'). Tin the tip, heat the pad and the leg\ntogether for two seconds, feed solder into the joint, not the iron. Twenty joints and"
        },
        {
          "bbox": [
            71.2,
            149.27,
            154.0,
            161.23
          ],
          "blockIndex": 4,
          "blockType": "paragraph",
          "confidence": "EXACT",
          "pageNumber": 3,
          "text": "you'll have it."
        },
        {
          "bbox": [
            71.2,
            167.1,
            540.4,
            203.83
          ],
          "blockIndex": 5,
          "blockType": "paragraph",
          "confidence": "EXACT",
          "pageNumber": 3,
          "text": "THE TRAP\nWaiting until a project 'needs' soldering. Breadboards fall apart the moment you move\nthem — soldering is what makes something yours to keep."
        },
        {
          "bbox": [
            71.2,
            209.7,
            529.36,
            246.43
          ],
          "blockIndex": 6,
          "blockType": "paragraph",
          "confidence": "EXACT",
          "pageNumber": 3,
          "text": "YOU'RE DONE WHEN\nYour joints look like small shiny cones, not grey blobs, and a soldered LED circuit\nworks first try."
        },
        {
          "bbox": [
            71.2,
            276.29,
            464.5,
            302.16
          ],
          "blockIndex": 7,
          "blockType": "project_boundary_heading",
          "confidence": "EXACT",
          "pageNumber": 3,
          "text": "STEP 05\nMeasure everything. Multimeter first, oscilloscope later."
        },
        {
          "bbox": [
            71.2,
            305.8,
            529.36,
            342.53
          ],
          "blockIndex": 8,
          "blockType": "paragraph",
          "confidence": "EXACT",
          "pageNumber": 3,
          "text": "DO THIS\nA $15 multimeter answers 90% of beginner questions: is there voltage here, is this\nwire actually connected (continuity beep), how much current does this draw. Measure"
        },
        {
          "bbox": [
            71.2,
            344.37,
            523.84,
            370.13
          ],
          "blockIndex": 9,
          "blockType": "paragraph",
          "confidence": "EXACT",
          "pageNumber": 3,
          "text": "your LED circuit and compare with what Ohm's law predicted. Only reach for a scope\nwhen you start caring about signals over time (PWM, serial, audio)."
        },
        {
          "bbox": [
            71.2,
            376.0,
            540.4,
            412.73
          ],
          "blockIndex": 10,
          "blockType": "paragraph",
          "confidence": "EXACT",
          "pageNumber": 3,
          "text": "THE TRAP\nGuessing. 'It doesn't work' is not a diagnosis. 'Pin 13 is at 4.9 V but the LED anode\nis at 0 V' is — and that takes ten seconds with a meter."
        },
        {
          "bbox": [
            71.2,
            418.6,
            363.76,
            441.53
          ],
          "blockIndex": 11,
          "blockType": "paragraph",
          "confidence": "EXACT",
          "pageNumber": 3,
          "text": "YOU'RE DONE WHEN\nYou debug by measuring before you debug by re-wiring."
        },
        {
          "bbox": [
            71.2,
            471.39,
            402.4,
            497.26
          ],
          "blockIndex": 12,
          "blockType": "project_boundary_heading",
          "confidence": "EXACT",
          "pageNumber": 3,
          "text": "STEP 06\nBuild one real project you actually want to use."
        },
        {
          "bbox": [
            71.2,
            500.9,
            534.88,
            551.43
          ],
          "blockIndex": 13,
          "blockType": "paragraph",
          "confidence": "EXACT",
          "pageNumber": 3,
          "text": "DO THIS\nNot a tutorial — something with a job: a plant-moisture alarm, a desk lamp that dims\nwith a knob, a door sensor that texts you, a temperature logger for your room. Pick\none, make a parts list, build it on a breadboard, then solder it onto perfboard and"
        },
        {
          "bbox": [
            71.2,
            553.27,
            159.52,
            565.23
          ],
          "blockIndex": 14,
          "blockType": "paragraph",
          "confidence": "EXACT",
          "pageNumber": 3,
          "text": "put it in a box."
        },
        {
          "bbox": [
            71.2,
            571.1,
            523.84,
            594.03
          ],
          "blockIndex": 15,
          "blockType": "paragraph",
          "confidence": "EXACT",
          "pageNumber": 3,
          "text": "THE TRAP\nTen half-finished projects. One finished thing you use every day teaches more than"
        },
        {
          "bbox": [
            71.2,
            595.87,
            330.64,
            607.83
          ],
          "blockIndex": 16,
          "blockType": "paragraph",
          "confidence": "EXACT",
          "pageNumber": 3,
          "text": "ten demos, and it's the one you'll show people."
        },
        {
          "bbox": [
            71.2,
            613.7,
            523.84,
            636.63
          ],
          "blockIndex": 17,
          "blockType": "paragraph",
          "confidence": "EXACT",
          "pageNumber": 3,
          "text": "YOU'RE DONE WHEN\nIt's been running on your desk for a week and you've fixed at least one thing that"
        },
        {
          "bbox": [
            71.2,
            638.47,
            104.32,
            650.43
          ],
          "blockIndex": 18,
          "blockType": "paragraph",
          "confidence": "EXACT",
          "pageNumber": 3,
          "text": "broke."
        }
      ],
